# Netrunner — Terraform overlay

Platform layout/CI: `app-terraform`.

## Naming / state

- Pattern: `[environment]-netrunner-[purpose]-[resource-type]` (e.g. `stg-netrunner-site-bucket`).
- State bucket: `shared-netrunner-terraform-state-bucket`; keys `envs/stg/`, `envs/prod/`, `cloudflare/`, `grafana/`. Bootstrap root uses **local** state (creates that bucket).
- Bootstrap first apply: `terraform init -reconfigure` → `apply` — see `infra/terraform/aws/bootstrap/README.md`.
- Plan role: `shared-netrunner-terraform-plan-role` + GitHub Environment `terraform`.
- AWS provider `default_tags`: `Project = "netrunner"` (plus `Environment`) on every taggable resource — filter by this tag in the console when sharing an account with Block Drop.

## Domains

| Env | Domain |
|-----|--------|
| stg | `netrunner-stg.7oas7er.com` |
| prod | `netrunner.7oas7er.com` |

## App-specific

- GitHub OIDC provider is **account-wide** (one URL → one IAM provider). Stg and prod both **look it up**; do not create a second provider when sharing an AWS account with Block Drop.
- **No Lambda / no `/api/scores`** — static S3 + CloudFront only.
- Cloudflare Terraform manages **DNS only** for the two Netrunner hostnames. Zone rulesets / SSL live in [`7oas7er/platform`](https://github.com/7oas7er/platform) `shared-edge` (one ruleset per phase — never recreate in an app root).
- **Origin-verify**: set `netrunner_*_origin_verify_secret` in platform `shared-edge` tfvars; keep AWS `origin_verify_secret` in sync. See `infra/terraform/cloudflare/README.md`.
- Local CF apply needs `export CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=…` (not tfvars).
- Access logs: `{env}-netrunner-access-logs-bucket` (CloudFront v2 + S3 site). CF 5xx alarms in `us-east-1`.
